137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Both tests agree that the series is already stationary at the level, which at first appears surprising for a series with a visible daily rhythm. This is not a contradiction: ADF and KPSS test for a stochastic trend \(a unit root\) and long-run drift, not for the presence of seasonality itself. A series can have a strong, stable, repeating seasonal pattern and still be stationary in the ADF/KPSS sense, because the pattern does not change the series' long-run mean or variance. This is confirmed by the ACF plots \(Figure 3\): the level series shows a slowly decaying autocorrelation with a clear peak recurring every 24 lags, the signature of stable daily seasonality rather than a unit root.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
