/E (All eight models \(five benchmarks, SARIMAX, the feature-based model, and the foundation model\) are evaluated on exactly the same 336-hour test window using the same four metrics, so that comparisons are on equal footing. MASE is used as the primary ranking metric because it is scale-free and directly interpretable relative to a seasonal-naive baseline \(MASE < 1 means the model beats seasonal-naive forecasting, in-sample\); RMSE and MAE are reported for completeness and because RMSE is more sensitive to the large occasional spikes that characterise this series; Bias indicates systematic over- or under- forecasting.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
