443 0 obj
<<
/Title (Chronos was evaluated zero-shot, target-only, and well beyond its recommended 64-step length for a single 336- step forecast. A rolling-origin evaluation with shorter horizons, or a covariate-aware variant \(Chronos-2\), would  be fairer. A single train/test split \(final 14 days\) was used rather than multiple rolling-origin folds; cross-validated evaluation  would give a more robust performance estimate. SARIMAX residuals indicate the linear Gaussian assumption fits this heavy-tailed, skewed error distribution  poorly; a model built for spike-heavy data \(e.g. a quantile-based ensemble\) may represent it better. An ablation of SARIMAX with/without exogenous weather variables was not run; this would quantify their value  for SARIMAX, mirroring the importance analysis already available for XGBoost.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 505 0 R
/Next 335 0 R
>>
endobj
